---
import './memory.css';
import {replay} from './model.mjs';
const steps=replay().slice(1,7);
---
<figure class="memory-figure">
 <div class="figure-heading"><span class="figure-number">Figure 1</span>Six requests need only two cards</div>
 <div class="scene">
  <div class="stats"><span><strong>4</strong> hits</span><span><strong>2</strong> source reads</span><span><strong>2</strong> resident cards</span></div>
  <ol class="requests">{steps.map(step=><li><span>Request {step.request.number}: <strong>{step.request.id}</strong></span><span>{step.hit?'Hit':'Source → fill'}</span><span class="resident-list">In cache: {step.residents.map(item=>item.id).join(', ')}</span></li>)}</ol>
  <div class="box"><strong>Authoritative catalogue</strong>P7, P3, P8, P9, P40 and other products remain here.</div>
  <p class="callout">The first request for each card does the source work. Four later requests reuse those two copies.</p>
 </div>
 <figcaption>The first six requests of this article’s invented trace, starting empty. P7 is the north shop’s blue mug, GBP 20.00. All product keys use v1, north, en-GB and GBP; the diagram shortens them to IDs. Requests finish in order, with immediate successful fills and no expiry or updates.</figcaption>
</figure>
<style>
 .requests { list-style:none;padding:0;margin:1rem 0; }
 .requests li { display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.3fr 1fr 1.4fr;gap:.5rem;padding:.55rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-rule); }
 .resident-list { color:var(--color-text-secondary); }
 @media(max-width:540px){.requests li{grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;}.resident-list{grid-column:1/-1;}}
</style>
